<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kadi Burhan al-Din state</h1><p class="st-meta">1381 CE – 1398 CE · capital Sivas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The sultanate of a judge and poet who seized the Eretnid throne and held central Anatolia against the Ottomans, Mamluks and Turkmen.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kadi-burhan-al-din">Kadi Burhan al-Din</a> Ahmad was a jurist from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayseri">Kayseri</a> who served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eretnids">Eretnids</a> as judge and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a>. As the dynasty weakened he became the real power, and in 1381, after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-al-din-ali">Ala al-Din Ali</a>, he declared himself sultan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>He spent his reign fighting: against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, whom he defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kirkdilim">Kirkdilim</a> in 1392, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutahharten">Mutahharten of Erzincan</a> and the beys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amasya">Amasya</a>. He was also a poet whose divan of Turkish verse is one of the earliest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, and his court historian Astarabadi wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bazm-u-razm">Bazm u Razm</a>, a chronicle of his reign in Persian.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1398 he was killed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-yuluk-osman">Qara Yuluk Osman</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sivas">Sivas</a> surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a>, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> destroyed it in 1400.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1381 CE – 1398 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.18%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1381 CE – 1398 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sivas</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kadi Burhan al-Din</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Turkish, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sultanate of Kadi Burhan al-Din</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1390&amp;focus=kadi-burhan-al-din-state" aria-label="Kadi Burhan al-Din state on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5593 755 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kadi Burhan al-Din state lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5913 1011L5913 1011M5913 1011L6003 1071M5913 1011L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5913 1011h0M6003 1071h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5913 1011h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5913 1011h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sivas. <a href="/atlas?year=1390&amp;focus=kadi-burhan-al-din-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
